COLUMNS
int ID
string Name // the zone light's name ("Durotar", "Stormwind", "Elwynn Redridge Zone Light", ...): proven from the bytes
int MapID // the Map row the polygon lies on: proven from the bytes (its points lie on that map's world: the TaxiNodes of the cities named fall inside the polygons named after them)
int LightID // the Light row whose LightParams the polygon applies: a Light row on every readable row (proven from the bytes; Classic Beta has one whose Light row is in a section it cannot decrypt); that the camera's polygon picks the light is inferred
int Field_03 // not established (0, 1 or 2 in Retail; 0 in Classic Beta and MoP Classic)
float Zmin // the lowest height in yards the polygon applies at (-64000: no limit): proven from the bytes as a height range (Zmin < Zmax on every row); applying it to the camera's height is inferred
float Zmax // the highest height in yards (64000: no limit): as Zmin
int TransitionType // 0 to 3 in Retail (0 on 686 of 735 rows, 1 on 43, 2 on 4, 3 on 2), 0 on every Classic Beta row: proven from the bytes; of the 352 Retail polygon pairs where one lies wholly inside the other (the strict test: every vertex of the smaller inside the larger, on the same map, and no edges crossing), the inner one's is higher on 56, lower on 1 and equal on 295 (a priority, inferred). The name is the public definitions', not proven; Classic Era's and MoP Classic's layout has no such column (it reads as 0)
int PlayerConditionID // 0, or a player condition (Retail: 39 rows, 33 of them on Eastern Kingdoms): the values are proven from the bytes; that a polygon with a condition applies only in a phase is the public definitions' name, not proven
int EraMoPField06 // not established (Classic Era and MoP Classic only: signed 2 bits, 0 on every MoP Classic row)
int EraMoPField07 // not established (Classic Era and MoP Classic only: 1 bit, 0 on every MoP Classic row)

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md, and the outdoor light, docs/world-viewer/10-light-sky-fog.md). The layouts come
COMMENT from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column the catalogue reads (database.xml, table ZoneLight)
COMMENT was checked against the clients' own bytes; the others are named by their field index, their types and widths the
COMMENT hypotheses' (never read). A neutral name that two layouts share is the same slot in the column order, not an
COMMENT established equal meaning; BA8274F0 has no PlayerConditionID and no TransitionType (each reads as 0). A polygon's
COMMENT points are ZoneLightPoint rows. Polygons nest (Retail: 357 pairs on one map lie wholly inside another by their
COMMENT vertices -- every vertex of the smaller inside the larger --, 352 of them with no edges crossing either), so a
COMMENT position can lie in several. Classic Beta keeps one row in an encrypted section it has no key for; it reads as
COMMENT zeros and is skipped. A layout not listed here is not read.

